---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — BCAway"
  description="Privacy Policy for BCAway iOS, Android, and Web applications. Operated by Savera Continental LTD. and developed by Kabir Sekhon."
>
  <main class="policy-page">
    <div class="policy-wrapper">
      <nav class="policy-nav">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <line x1="19" y1="12" x2="5" y2="12"></line>
            <polyline points="12 19 5 12 12 5"></polyline>
          </svg>
          Back to BCAway
        </a>
      </nav>

      <header class="policy-header">
        <div class="logo-small">
          <Logo width={48} />
        </div>
        <h1 class="policy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy-meta">Last Updated: September 24, 2026 • Effective Immediately</p>
      </header>

      <div class="policy-content">
        <div class="callout-box">
          <p>
            <strong>Summary:</strong> BCAway is engineered with a strict privacy-first, minimal-data ethos. To protect faculty data, access to teacher absence information is restricted to verified Bergen County Academies students using their official <code>@bergen.org</code> school email. We do <strong>not</strong> collect passwords, do <strong>not</strong> track your personal location, do <strong>not</strong> sync your class schedule to our servers, do <strong>not</strong> access school gradebooks, and <strong>never</strong> sell or monetize user data.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>1. Introduction & Overview</h2>
          <p>
            This Privacy Policy applies to the <strong>BCAway</strong> mobile applications (iOS and Android) and web application (<a href="https://app.bcaway.app">app.bcaway.app</a>), published by <strong>Savera Continental LTD.</strong> and developed by <strong>Kabir Sekhon</strong> (collectively referred to as "we", "us", or "our").
          </p>
          <p>
            BCAway is an independent student utility created to display teacher absences and daily bell schedules for Bergen County Academies ("BCA"). By accessing or using BCAway, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>2. Information We Collect and How It Is Handled</h2>
          <p>We practice strict data minimization. We only collect the minimal technical data required to authenticate students, secure faculty absence information, and deliver core utility features:</p>

          <h3>A. School Email Address & Authentication Records</h3>
          <p>
            To prevent unauthorized external access to faculty attendance records, students must authenticate using their official school email address (ending strictly in <code>@bergen.org</code>).
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Passwordless Verification:</strong> We do not collect, require, or store passwords. Sign-in is handled via a secure, single-use confirmation link (magic link) dispatched directly to your school email address.</li>
            <li><strong>Supabase Authentication:</strong> Your email address is stored in our secure Supabase authentication database (<code>auth.users</code>), accompanied by an internal UUID, account creation timestamp, and last login timestamp.</li>
            <li><strong>Strict Domain Restriction:</strong> Our backend database triggers and Row-Level Security (RLS) policies enforce that only verified <code>@bergen.org</code> accounts can register or query teacher absence data. Non-school emails are systematically rejected.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>B. Local On-Device Data (Stored Exclusively on Your Device)</h3>
          <p>
            BCAway is designed to keep your personal schedule configuration local to your device:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Session Credentials:</strong> Encrypted JWT access and refresh tokens are stored in your device's sandboxed local storage (<code>AsyncStorage</code> on mobile, <code>localStorage</code> on web) so you remain securely logged in across launches.</li>
            <li><strong>Schedule Customization:</strong> Your configured courses, custom mod labels, and free-period preferences are saved locally on your physical device and are <strong>never</strong> transmitted to or stored on our servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Teacher Subscriptions:</strong> Any specific teachers you select to receive tailored absence alerts for are tracked entirely locally on your device.</li>
            <li><strong>Local Absence Cache:</strong> Absence records and master bell schedules are cached locally on your device to enable offline viewing and ensure immediate load times.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>C. Push Notification Device Tokens (Optional)</h3>
          <p>
            If you choose to enable push notifications (such as morning absence announcements or personalized alerts when your tracked teachers are absent), your device generates an anonymous push token:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Delivery Services:</strong> Apple Push Notification service (APNs) for iOS and Google Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) for Android.</li>
            <li><strong>Anonymity:</strong> Push notification tokens are randomized strings and are never linked to your personal identity, student ID, device IMEI, or physical location.</li>
            <li><strong>Revocation:</strong> You can disable notifications at any time directly through the app settings or via your device's system notification preferences.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>D. Technical Log Data & Network Telemetry</h3>
          <p>
            When requesting absence or schedule updates, standard non-identifying HTTP request headers (such as timestamp, operating system, app version, and IP address) are processed in real time by our edge infrastructure (Cloudflare and Supabase) solely for DDoS mitigation, rate limiting, and network firewall defense. We do not use this data for behavioral profiling or tracking.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>3. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
          <p>We are dedicated to safeguarding student privacy. BCAway does <strong>NOT</strong> collect, request, or store:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>No user passwords or biometric data.</li>
            <li>No student real names, home addresses, or phone numbers.</li>
            <li>No student ID numbers or lunch account codes.</li>
            <li>No student grades, GPA, transcripts, or academic performance records.</li>
            <li>No integration or login credentials for school management systems (such as Genesis, PowerSchool, Google Classroom, Naviance, or Canvas).</li>
            <li>No personal daily schedules or classroom assignments on our backend servers.</li>
            <li>No GPS coordinates, Wi-Fi location tracking, or Bluetooth beacons.</li>
            <li>No access to your camera, microphone, photo library, or address book.</li>
            <li>No advertising identifiers (IDFA, GAID) or cross-site tracking cookies.</li>
            <li>No data monetization or sale of student data to third parties.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>4. How We Use Information</h2>
          <p>The information we collect is used strictly for the following purposes:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Verifying active Bergen County Academies enrollment prior to displaying teacher absence information.</li>
            <li>Maintaining your persistent authenticated session on your device.</li>
            <li>Delivering push notification alerts that you have opted into.</li>
            <li>Enforcing API rate limits and preventing automated scraping or unauthorized database access.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>5. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
          <p>
            We rely on trusted, industry-standard infrastructure providers solely to host our backend database, secure authentication, and route network requests. These providers adhere to strict data security standards:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Supabase Inc.:</strong> Hosts our user authentication system, session management, and PostgreSQL database with Row-Level Security (RLS).</li>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare Inc.:</strong> Provides serverless API routing, global content caching, and DDoS protection.</li>
            <li><strong>Apple Inc. (APNs) & Google LLC (FCM):</strong> Delivers encrypted push notifications to iOS and Android devices.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not sell, rent, lease, trade, or share any student information with data brokers, advertisers, or third-party marketing companies.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>6. Children's Privacy (COPPA & FERPA Compliance)</h2>
          <p>
            BCAway is designed for high school students attending Bergen County Academies and operates in full compliance with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) standards:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>We do not collect personal information from children under the age of 13.</li>
            <li>We do not access, process, or maintain student educational records or academic histories.</li>
            <li>Student school email addresses are processed solely for the narrow purpose of school domain verification and access authorization.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>7. Data Retention, Sign-Out, and Account Deletion</h2>
          <p>
            You have full control over your session and account data:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Signing Out:</strong> You can sign out at any time through the app by visiting <em>Settings &rarr; Account &rarr; Sign Out</em>. Signing out immediately invalidates your session and removes local auth tokens and cached absences from your device.</li>
            <li><strong>Account Deletion:</strong> If you wish to permanently delete your <code>@bergen.org</code> authentication record and associated push tokens from our Supabase database, you can submit a deletion request by emailing <a href="mailto:kabsek30@bergen.org">kabsek30@bergen.org</a> from your school email. Requests are processed promptly.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>8. Non-Affiliation and Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>BCAway is an independent student utility and is NOT affiliated with, authorized by, endorsed by, or in any way officially connected with Bergen County Academies (BCA), the Bergen County Technical School District (BCTS), the Bergen County Board of Education, or any of their subsidiaries or affiliates.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            Neither Bergen County Academies nor Bergen County Technical Schools is responsible or liable for the operation, privacy practices, or data handling of BCAway. For complete legal terms, please review our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service and Disclaimers</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions, feedback, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us:
          </p>
          <div class="contact-card">
            <p><strong>Publisher:</strong> Savera Continental LTD.</p>
            <p><strong>Developer:</strong> Kabir Sekhon</p>
            <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:kabsek30@bergen.org">kabsek30@bergen.org</a></p>
            <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://bcaway.app">bcaway.app</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <footer class="policy-footer">
        <div class="footer-links-group">
          <a href="/" class="footer-back-link">Return to Home</a>
          <span class="footer-sep">•</span>
          <a href="/terms" class="footer-back-link">Terms & Disclaimers</a>
          <span class="footer-sep">•</span>
          <a href="/contact" class="footer-back-link">Contact</a>
        </div>
        <p class="copyright-text">
          &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} Kabir Sekhon. All rights reserved.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-page {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 48px 20px 60px;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .policy-wrapper {
    max-width: 680px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .policy-nav {
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .policy-header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .logo-small {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .policy-title {
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text-main);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .policy-meta {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .callout-box {
    background-color: var(--color-primary-light);
    border: 1px solid #BFDBFE;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: #1E3A8A;
  }

  .callout-box code {
    font-size: 13px;
    background-color: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.1);
    padding: 2px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .policy-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-main);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .policy-section h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-main);
    margin: 16px 0 8px;
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #374151;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .policy-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-section ul {
    margin: 8px 0 16px 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .policy-section li {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #374151;
  }

  .policy-section code {
    font-size: 13px;
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 2px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .policy-section a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .policy-section a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary-hover);
  }

  .contact-card {
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .contact-card p {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .policy-footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: 28px;
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .footer-links-group {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .copyright-text {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .footer-back-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .footer-sep {
    color: var(--color-border);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .policy-page {
      padding: 32px 16px 48px;
    }

    .policy-title {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
